Python Control Flow :
Title: Largest of three numbers

Concept:
List comprehension is a compact way to create lists in Python.
Instead of writing multiple lines using for loops and append(), you can generate a new list in one line.
It’s faster and improves code readability.

Tech used :
Language : pyhton
Compiler : Visual Studio Code

Logic Flow:
new_list = [expression for item in iterable if condition]
expression → value or operation you want to store in the list
item → each element from the iterable (like list, tuple, etc.)
condition → optional filter to include only certain elements

Input :
# List Comprehension Example
lst_1 = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 66, 8, 9, 94]

# Extract only even numbers
even = [i for i in lst_1 if i % 2 == 0]

Output :
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 66, 8, 9, 94]


print(even)
